<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2012/Simon-SP.jpg" alt="A self portrait in charcoal of artist Simon Bland " width="600" height="485" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Self portrait from life. &nbsp;2012.</p>
<p>I used homemade charcoal made from some honeysuckle vines that were cut down last year. &nbsp;I wrapped the vines in foil and cooked them in the barbeque at 400F for three hours.</p>
<p>I was able to get four values from the charcoal alone. The slightly off-white paper provided another value and a white conte crayon gave me the lightest value. &nbsp;That's six total.</p>
<p>The half-lit face is much easier to draw than a three-quarter lit face.</p>